        }
      ],
      "answer": "In the MapleHarvest Quebec pilot, the temporary field mappings planned in the router transform include mapping txn_id to transaction_id, total_amount to amount_cents, applying type coercion from string to int, preserving key fields store_id and register_id, and adding a transformation flag field _ns_transform=true. This transform is to be deployed in the SI-CLOUD-ROUTER component as a temporary measure to address schema rejection issues caused by mixed field names and types from store-level preprocessing. The transform will also enable OR-AUDIT-LOGS for each transformed event to ensure compliance and traceability.\n\nThe March 23 workshop is a Schema Signoff Workshop with the agenda to agree on a canonical schema for payment, register_events, and sensor_thermo data; define alias mapping; and establish a producer migration plan. The deliverable from this workshop is a signed schema document to be uploaded to SI-SCHEMA-REG and a change control ticket with producer migration milestones. The workshop is scheduled for 90 minutes and includes key stakeholders such as Sophie Tremblay, Marc Gauthier, Ellen Park, Platform engineers, and Northstar SE/Ing teams [art_5a91258f4056].",
