      "answer": "The customer most likely to defect to a cheaper tactical competitor if the next promised milestone is missed is Pioneer Freight Solutions. They are currently running a tactical proof of concept (PoC) of NoiseGuard as a cheaper alternative for immediate tactical needs related to manual deduplication and alert noise reduction [art_ac8afb52f2d3, art_7373b64fdfdd, art_a504e4c5b6f8].\n\nThe exact milestone critical to Pioneer Freight Solutions is the acceptance of the remediation plan milestones addressing the taxonomy change incident. These milestones include:\n\n- Schema verification by 2026-03-22\n- Shadow index build from 2026-03-29 to 2026-04-09\n- Backfill and index rebuild from 2026-04-12 to 2026-04-30\n- Validation window from 2026-05-01 to 2026-05-14\n\nFailure to meet these milestones triggers a one-time credit of 10% of the annual contract value as a commercial concession [art_7373b64fdfdd, art_a504e4c5b6f8].\n\nNo evidence identifies any other customer with a similar risk profile or competing milestone commitments to compare likelihood of defection, nor are there additional details on exact milestone definitions beyond those dates and acceptance criteria for other customers or competitors.",
